Test the echo model kept at a call's start

WebRTC patch 0018 keeps AEC3's echo model at a call's start, until the linear filter first
takes echo away, while the other side plays without pauses, at an echo path gain no higher
than the microphone heard. In test/echo_music_start.test.cc AEC3 hears 8 s from a call's
start: music through speakers, 10 and 20 dB under the other side, comes out at least 0.3
dB quieter than with the patch left out (Fogata-Aec3KeepEchoModelWhileErleIsLow/margin:0/,
stock AEC3), and 0.6 dB quieter with pauses:0.1; a voice through speakers no louder than
0.5 dB over stock; with a headset and music, the room's noise and the person's words go
out within 0.2 dB of stock; and the person's words over music, and over a voice with the
default setting, are held down no more than 0.5 dB beyond stock. Built in again: the
library shows only its own API.

